<select> and date/time inputs open the HarmonyOS shell's own pickers.

Android shows a <select> and the date, time, month and week inputs with
system pickers; OHOS fell through to Blink's desktop dropdown and calendar,
which are small and fiddly on a phone. On the phone UI the engine now
- turns on kOhosExternalPopupMenus (defined here in chrome_client_impl.cc),
  so a <select> uses ExternalPopupMenu, and RenderFrameHostImpl hands the
  menu to a handler chrome registers (content/public/browser/
  ohos_popup_menu.h, in the overlay) instead of a RenderViewHostDelegateView
  that only exists with USE_EXTERNAL_POPUP_MENU;
- has date inputs use ExternalDateTimeChooser (ohos-shell-date-picker.patch),
  served by chrome::ohos::BindAuraShellDateTimeChooser, which
  ohos-web-share.patch binds.
Both send the request to the shell as runtime events.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-native-pickers.patch

